<title>UK: Sears weak as Merrill Lynch downgrades.</title>
<headline>Sears weak as Merrill Lynch downgrades.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Sears Plc were weak in a rising UK equity market on Wednesday as analysts at Merrill Lynch rated the stock &quot;reduce&quot; and lowered earnings estimates, market sources said.</p>
<p>Shares in the retail group were down 1/2p at 91-1/2 by 1149 GMT in active trading of 4.6 million shares. By contrast the FTSE 100 index of blue chip stocks was up 34.7 points at 4,014.3.</p>
</text>
